## 2. The Stable Limit Is Forced

On a smooth elliptic curve, rank two and degree three are coprime. Atiyah's
classification implies that a stable bundle of rank two and degree three is
uniquely determined by its determinant. The middle term in (1) is stable by
`UST.G3G`, and

\[
 \det M_j=P\otimes N=\det(P\oplus N).
\]

Thus it is the unique stable fixed-determinant limit of the punctured family.
There is no new continuous choice. The extension space has dimension three,
but changing a nonzero extension representative does not change the stable
middle bundle with this determinant. The three locked Koszul representatives
(s_0,s_1,s_2) record the qutrit linearization, not three physical moduli.

The original family has class (t e_j). On (t\ne0), scaling the subobject
identifies (t e_j) with (e_j), so the original and repaired families are
holomorphically isomorphic on the punctured disc. At (t=0), the repaired
family has the nonsplit stable limit (1), rather than the split mixed-WIT
limit.

There are exactly two simple zeros and their tubular neighborhoods can be
chosen disjoint. Gluing the repaired family on each neighborhood to the
original family on their complement therefore requires only pairwise overlap
maps. Ordinary holomorphic bundle gluing produces the repaired local family;
perfect-complex descent gives the same construction in the alpha-twisted
derived category.

